e of ingestion.  Very hazardous in case of eye contact (irritant), of inhalation.  Severe\nover-exposure can result in death.  Inflammation of the eye is characterized by redness, watering, and itching.\nPotential Chronic Health\nEffects\nExtremely hazardous in case of ingestion.\nVery hazardous in case of eye contact (irritant), of inhalation.\nCARCINOGENIC EFFECTS: Not available.\nMUTAGENIC EFFECTS: Not available.\nTERATOGENIC EFFECTS: Not available.\nDEVELOPMENTAL TOXICITY: Not available.\nThe substance is toxic to kidneys, liver.\nRepeated or prolonged exposure to the substance can produce target organs damage.  Repeated exposure to an\nhighly toxic material may produce general deterioration of health by an accumulation in one or many human\norgans.\nContinued on Next Page--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSanta Cruz Biotechnology, Inc. (https://datasheets.scbt.com/sds/aghs/en/sc-236924.pdf)\nciteturn46search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.0 years ago; Na2SeO4•10H2O\nChemical Name Sodium selenate decahydrate | CAS No 10102-23-5 | Weight % >98 | Oral LD50 - | Dermal LD50 - | Inhalation LC50 - --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---4.\nRevision date  26-Oct-2015\nSC-236924 -  Sodium selenate decahydrate\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________\nHazards not otherwise classified (HNOC)\nHazards not otherwise classified (HNOC)\nNot applicable\nOther Information\n4\nNFPA\nHMIS\nHealth hazards\n4\nFlammability\n0\nHealth hazards\nFlammability\n0\nStability\nPhysical hazards\n0\n0\n-\nPersonal protection\n-\nPhysical and chemical\nproperties\n3. COMPOSITION/INFORMATION ON INGREDIENTS\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________\nCAS No\n10102-23-5\nMolecular Weight\n369.09\nFormula\nNa2SeO4•10H2O\nChemical Name Sodium selenate decahydrate | CAS No 10102-23-5 | Weight % >98 | Or