 - Technical Data Sheet (https://www.chemicalbook.com/tds-coa/sodium-selenate-decahydrate.htm)\nciteturn46search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Product Name: Sodium selenate decahydrate\n\nCAS No.: 10102-23-5\n\n# Technical Data Sheet Sodium selenate decahydrate\n\nCompound Information\n\nProduct Name: Sodium selenate decahydrate\n\nCAS No.: 10102-23-5\n\nMolecular Formula: H5NaO5Se\n\nMolecular Weight: 187\n\nRevision Date: 2026-04-15\n\nAnalytical Information\n\nTests  | Specifications\n--- | ---\nAppearance  | White moist crystals\nIdentification (ICP)  | Confirms with sodium and selenium components\nGravimetric Analysis  | 17.7 - 25.1% (SE)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSodium selenate (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodium_selenate)\nciteturn46search17 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; CAS Number ... Solubility in water ... The decahydrate is a common ingredient in multivitamins and livestock feed as a source of selenium. ... The sodium selenite is oxidized in a basic medium hydrogen peroxide to form a selenate, which is then spray-dried. ... Sodium selenate is effectively used for bio-fortification of crops hence fortifying food/feed to mitigate selenium deficiency in humans and livestock. ... \"Similarities and peculiarities between the crystal structures of the hydrates of sodium sulfate and selenate\".\nSodium selenate\nSodium selenate\n\n Names \n IUPAC name \n\nSodium selenate\n\n Identifiers \n\nCAS Number\n\n  | \n\n* 10102-23-5^{  X mark }\n\n3D model (JSmol)\n\n  | \n\n* Interactive image\n\n ChEBI  | \n\n* CHEBI:77775^{  check }\n\n ChEMBL  | \n\n* ChEMBL114503\n\n ChemSpider  | \n\n* 24185\n\n DrugBank  | \n\n* DBSALT002579\n\n ECHA InfoCard  | 100.033.169  \n EC Number  | \n\n* 236-501-8\n\nPubChem CID\n\n  | \n\n* 25960\n\n RTECS number  | \n\n* VS6650000\n\n UNII  | \n\n* decahydrate: 0CJN4029EB^{  check }\n\n UN number  | 2630 \n\nCompTox Dashboard (EPA)\n\n  | \n\n* DTXSID5032076 \n\nInChI\n\n* \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSodium selenate decahydrate-India Fine Chemicals (https://www.indiafinechemicals.com/en/products/detail/5909)\nciteturn46search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # Sodium selenate decahydrate\n\nCAS RN🄬  | 10102-23-5\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCrystal structures of Na2SeO4·1.5H2O and Na2SeO4·10H2O (https://journals.iucr.org/e/issues/2014/08/00/hb0010/)\nciteturn46search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.3 years ago; Crawled: last month; The crystal structures of Na_{2}SeO_{4}·1.5H_{2}O (sodium selenate sesquihydrate) and Na_{2}SeO_{4}·10H_{2}O (sodium selenate deca­hydrate) are isotypic with those of Na_{2}CrO_{4}·1.5H_{2}O and Na_{2}X SeO_{4}·10H_{2}O (X = S, Cr), respectively. ... According to Rietveld refinements using TOPAS (Bruker, 2013) the product crystallized at 300 K consisted of Na_{2}SeO_{4} and Na_{2}SeO_{4}.1.5H_{2}O in an approximate 9:1 ratio, the product crystallized at 290 K consisted of Na_{2}SeO_{4} and Na_{2}SeO_{4}.1.5H_{2}O in an approximate 5:1 ratio, and the product crystallized at 280 K consisted of Na_{2}SeO_{4}, Na_{2}SeO_{4}.1.5H_{2}O and Na_{2}SeO_{4}.10H_{2}O in an approximate 5:4:1 ratio.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSodium selenate decahydrate | CAS 10102-23-5 | SCBT - Santa Cruz Biotechnology (https://www.scbt.com/p/sodium-selenate-decahydrate-10102-23-5)\nciteturn46search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; Image: Sodium selenate decahydrate (CAS 10102-23-5) - chemical structure image Molecular structure of Sodium selenate decahydrate, CAS Number: 10102-23-5 ... Sodium selenate decahydrate is an inorganic compound with high solubility in water.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSodium selenate decahydrate_Papers_Articles_Chemsrc (https://www.chemsrc.com/en/CasPaper/900955.html)\nciteturn46search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; # Sodium selenate decahydrate\n\nImage: Sodium selenate decahydrate Structure Sodium selenate decahydrate structure  | Common Name  | Sodium selenate decahydrate\nCAS Number  | 10102-23-5  | Molecular Weight  | 369.09000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSodium sulfate (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodium_sulfate)\nciteturn46search18 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; * Disodium sulfate ...  ChEBI  | ... * Sodium selenate ... With an annual production of 6 million tonnes, the decahydrate is a major commodity chemical product. ... The decahydrate of sodium sulfate is known as Glauber's salt after the Dutch–German chemist and apothecary Johann Rudolf Glauber (1604–1670), who discovered it in Austrian spring water in 1625.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIndium(III) selenate (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indium%28III%29_selenate)\nciteturn46search19 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; Indium(III) selenate can be prepared by dissolving indium(III) hydroxide in aqueous selenic acid and crystallizing the resulting solution. ... The original preparation gave white, readily water-soluble, hygroscopic crystals whose analysis corresponded approximately to a decahydrate, In_{2}(SeO_{4})_{3}·10H_{2}O. ... Phase-equilibrium studies have also been reported for indium selenate with lithium, sodium, potassium, rubidium, caesium and ammonium selenates.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSolubility table (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solubility_table)\nciteturn46search20 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 months ago;  Sodium selenate | Na_{2}SeO_{4} | 13.3 | 25.2 | 26.9 | 77 | 81.8 |  | 78.6 |  | 74.8 | 73 | 72.7 ...  Sodium tetraborate (decahydrate) | Na_{2}B_{4}O_{7}·10H_{2}O | 2 | 2.3 | 2.5 | 4 | 6 | 10 | 15 |  |  |  | 65.5\n",
